body:
Fixes #11140
Clause-②: no

## What

`MultiSelectField` is the widget that a `select` field declared `multiple: true` and a `multiselect` field both render. It read no `placeholder`, so it silently dropped the key that the single-value branch honours. Its editable chip row now shows the author's `placeholder` while the value is empty, and hides it after the first pick.

The direction is the triage ruling on the card (comment 5898770057, ENFORCE): honour the key. The catalog example `fields-select/multi-select` stays as written.

## How

- **Where it is read.** The widget reads `field?.placeholder`: the same key, from the same `field` carrier, that `SingleSelectField` hands its `SelectValue`. `placeholder` is declared on `BaseFieldMetadata`, so the read goes through the declared type and not the widget's `as any` alias. The widget contract declares no `placeholder` prop, and `toDomProps` drops the one the form renderer forwards, so the carrier is the one channel.
- **When it shows.** It shows while `selected.length === 0`. A `null` value counts as empty, because the widget already normalises it to an empty array. An empty string counts as no placeholder, the way the single branch's `||` reads it.
- **Markup.** One muted `span` is the first child of the chip container, carrying plain text only: no `aria-label`, no `id`, no `role`. The container keeps the host's `aria-labelledby`, the association PR objectui#11139 relies on. The `group` role does not take its name from content, so the placeholder never becomes the field's accessible name.
- **Other states are unchanged.**
  - Readonly and empty still renders `EmptyValue` (the "No value" mark). That is a different state from the editable empty one, and it is the state the accname comment in the readonly branch is about.
  - A list with zero offered options, or a gated list, still renders `OptionsEmptyState`.
  - Disabled is part of the editable branch, so it shows the placeholder, as a disabled native input and the Radix single select both do.
- **No stock fallback.** The single branch falls back to `common.selectOption`; this widget does not. Every option is already on screen as a chip, and a fallback would change how every existing multi-value field renders, on every host. I read the triage's control line ("a field with no `placeholder` renders the widget's default") as the unchanged chip row, and pinned it that way.

## Pins

- **Widget:** `packages/fields/src/widgets/MultiSelectField.placeholder-11140.test.tsx`, 8 cases:
  - it shows while empty;
  - a `null` value counts as empty;
  - it hides after a pick and comes back once the pick is undone;
  - it is absent when a value arrives already selected;
  - control: with no placeholder, the container holds only the chip buttons;
  - an empty string counts as none;
  - the group is still named by the host label, and the hint carries no aria, id or role attribute;
  - readonly and empty renders the empty-value mark, not the placeholder.
- **Catalog:** `examples/schema-catalog/test/fields-select-multi-placeholder-11140.test.tsx`, 4 cases through the real `SchemaRenderer`, the real form renderer and the real `@object-ui/fields` registration:
  - the example authors `Select tags...` beside `multiple: true`;
  - the text renders while the field is empty, is gone after a pick, and comes back on undo;
  - the group stays named by the field label;
  - control: with the key deleted, the group holds only chip buttons.

## Verification

Gates ran on branch head `01a20886b`, and each exit code was captured before any pipe. The only commit after the ablation adds the changeset.

- `pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 packages/fields/ examples/schema-catalog/` plus five cross-package files that render a multi-value field through a host: `form-builtin-select-multiple-11116.test.tsx`, `form-dependent-values.test.tsx`, `ActionParamDialog.test.tsx`, `bulkActionDialogParams.test.tsx`, `InlineFieldInput.capabilityWidgetRetired.test.tsx`. Result: `Test Files 263 passed | 1 skipped (264)`, `Tests 5790 passed | 7 skipped (5797)`, lock VERDICT command-exit 0.
- `pnpm --filter @object-ui/fields type-check` exits 0. Its test leg (`tsconfig.test.json`) lists the new widget test (`--listFiles`, 1 hit).
- `pnpm --filter @object-ui/example-schema-catalog type-check` exits 0, after building its dependency closure (28 tasks).
- eslint on the 3 changed source files: `--format json` reports 3 files, 0 errors, 7 warnings, all `no-explicit-any`. One of them is the widget's unchanged `field as any` line.
- These checks all exit 0:
  - `check-changeset-presence`: 1 changeset declared for 1 released package;
  - `check-control-bytes`;
  - `check-new-cross-file-line-citations`: 0 new;
  - `check-changeset-fixed`, `check-changeset-no-major`, `check-changeset-claims` and `check-pending-changeset-literals`;
  - `check-test-path-roots`;
  - the three `vi-mock` checks;
  - `check-type-check-coverage`.
- `check-governed-queue-guard --test` over the 4 paths answers NOT GOVERNED.

**Ablation.** It ran at the committed fix `94ff11cd6`, through `ablation-replace.mjs` in wrap mode. The mutation replaced the `field?.placeholder` read with `undefined`. The tool confirmed it on disk: anchor count 1 to 0, and the blob changed. Result: `Tests 5 failed | 7 passed (12)`. The 5 red cases are the placeholder-present ones: 4 widget cases and the catalog render case. The 7 green cases are the controls. Direction: red, as predicted. The restore was proven by blob == HEAD and an empty `git diff HEAD`.

**Declared narrowing.** I did not run the repo-wide `pnpm lint`; CI owns it. eslint ran on the changed files only. Its population is read from eslint's own resolved config (`--print-config` on each file), and its file count from the `--format json` output (3 files). No file's config sets `parserOptions.project` or `projectService`, so linting is not type-aware and this diff cannot move the verdict on any untouched file. Tests were narrowed to the fields package, the catalog and the five host files above. The full `pnpm test` belongs to CI.

## Acceptance notes

- **Observation, not filed.** This is a read-only trace, not measured, and has no carrier. On the object-bound form path, a form view's per-field `placeholder` override (the `placeholder` of a spec `FormFieldSchema` section entry) is written by `sectionFields` onto the FormField, while the `field` carrier stays the object's field metadata. A widget that reads `field.placeholder` sees the object field's placeholder, not the view's override. The `placeholder` prop the form renderer forwards is undeclared in `FieldWidgetComponentProps` and never reaches the DOM. This affects the single-value select and this widget alike, so this PR keeps the two in lockstep and does not widen either. It is filed nowhere, because nothing measured it at a public door.
- **NOT MEASURED:** a real browser render of the hint's visual placement (a muted inline span before the chips). All render evidence above comes from happy-dom through the real renderer.

